implementationPlan.description:
Create moe-jetbrains/src/test/resources/client-accounts.json with the Write tool (global rail: tracked files only through Edit/Write). It must be byte-identical to the architect's oracle output, /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc7-architect/client-accounts.json: sha256 e08b58c803980b2474bad79bd427069ebed688fdbf18f90ba6a3ac5c6c1295fc, 36335 bytes, LF, ASCII only with \u escapes.
- The oracle is gen.py in the same folder, an independent Python mirror of MoeJson.parseAccountRotation and AccountPresentation.kt at HEAD; fmt.py gives the compact layout.
- If the folder is gone, regenerate with `cd /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc7-architect && python3 -I gen.py raw.json && python3 -I fmt.py raw.json client-accounts.json`. It is deterministic and gives the same sha256.
- Read the file before writing it, and confirm `sha256sum` of the tracked copy.
Shape: `{ version: 1, now: "2026-10-20T12:00:00.000Z", zone: "UTC", rows: [...], labels: [...] }`.
- rows: `{ id C01..C15, note, rotation, selectedId, connected, expectRows, expectChips, expectActions }`. rotation is the daemon's AccountRotationView wire JSON (packages/moe-daemon/src/state/accountStore.ts accountRotationView) or null. expectRows entries are `{ id, position, label, signIn, fiveHour, weekly, status, vmToken }`; expectChips is a list of texts; expectActions holds the 12 AccountActions booleans.
- labels: `{ id L01..L14, input, valid }`.
- Every text is `{ "key", "args" }`, with args JSON strings or integers.
Row coverage:
- null rotation C01; empty list C02; unusable file (error chip, no actions) C03;
- one account C04, C13; several accounts C05, C12, C14;
- sign-in states subscription, signed_out and other: C05, C15;
- windows with and without a reset time: C05, C12, C14; the busiest seven_day* window: C05; a window without a percent: C13;
- the account in use: active C04, active with seats C05, in use C14;
- switch percent: C14 (switchAtPercent 75; spent comes from the daemon's blockedUntil), plus the switchAt flag in every row;
- vmToken set, not set and absent: C06, C07, C08 (rows and actions);
- disconnected C09;
- selection at the top, middle and bottom: C06, C07, C08; a missing selection C10;
- no cli C11;
- more than four subscription chips, a shortened label, floored percents and an other-day time: C12;
- non-ISO reset text shown as sent: C13;
- no subscription account: C15.
Label coverage: L01-L08 are valid ('', blanks, plain text, 64 chars, 64 chars padded, outer tab/newline trimmed, non-ASCII letters, an interior U+0085). L09-L14 are invalid (65 chars, an interior tab, newline, U+0000, U+001F, U+007F).
L08 is deliberate. The daemon's rule (packages/moe-daemon/src/accounts/registry.ts CONTROL_CHARS_RE = /[\u0000-\u001f\u007f]/) accepts C1 controls, but JetBrains' isISOControl refuses them. So L08 exposes the JetBrains bug that step 3 fixes.
Deliberately left out:
- leading or trailing U+001C..U+001F or U+FEFF, where Kotlin trim and JS trim disagree (mem:decision-client-corpus-conventions);
- the 32-account add limit, which AccountPresentationTest pins;
- wrong-kind wire values.
If you prove an oracle row wrong against AccountPresentation.kt, fix only that row and say why in the summary.

Write moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/AccountsCorpusTest.kt with the Write tool (package com.moe.toolwindow; JUnit 4 + Gson). Model it on DeliveryCorpusTest.kt: loadCorpus, and per-row failure collection.
Header KDoc:
- one client-neutral corpus; VS Code's VSC-13 (task-065e4812, tests/accounts-corpus.test.cjs) replays the same bytes through moe-vscode/src/util/AccountPresentation.ts, and VSC-15 checks its context keys against expectActions;
- the CQ-I06b rule: a disagreement is fixed or filed, never given a client-specific expectation.
Its error handling: a missing or unparseable resource throws an AssertionError naming it. A malformed or throwing row fails that row with a message. Each test ends in one assert that lists every failing id.
Use now = Instant.parse(corpus.now) and zone = ZoneId.of(corpus.zone).
Tests:
1. `the corpus is well formed`:
   - version 1; now and zone parse;
   - at least 12 rows with unique C[0-9]{2} ids, and at least 8 labels with unique L[0-9]{2} ids;
   - each row has a non-empty note, rotation null or an object, selectedId a string or null, and connected a boolean;
   - expectRows is an array of objects with exactly id, position, label, signIn, fiveHour, weekly, status and vmToken;
   - every text has exactly {key: string, args: array of JSON strings or integral numbers};
   - expectChips is an array of texts;
   - expectActions has exactly the 12 AccountActions member names (add, rename, moveUp, moveDown, removeOnly, signIn, signOut, signOutAndRemove, check, switchAt, setVmToken, removeVmToken), each a JSON boolean;
   - each label row has exactly id, input (string) and valid (boolean).
2. `every rotation row renders its rows, chips and actions`:
   - a non-null rotation goes through MoeJson.parseAccountRotation (the ACCOUNTS_UPDATED path in MoeMessageDispatcher) AND through MoeJson.parseState({"project":{"id":"proj-corpus","name":"corpus"},"accountRotation": rotation}).accountRotation (STATE_SNAPSHOT). Both must be non-null and equal, or the row fails;
   - compare AccountPresentation.rows(rotation, now, zone), chips(rotation, now, zone) and actions(rotation, selectedId, connected) with the expectations, built as AccountRow/AccountText/AccountActions data classes. A JSON integer arg becomes an Int via BigDecimal(asString).intValueExact(), and a JSON string becomes a String, so 92 and "92" never compare equal;
   - collect `<id>: <which> expected <e>, got <a>` and finish with one assertEquals.
3. `every label case follows the daemon rule`: AccountPresentation.isValidLabel(input) == valid for every label row, with one assertEquals over the failing ids.
4. `corpus text keys are exactly the bundle's account presentation keys`:
   - load messages/MoeBundle.properties through the classloader;
   - every key the corpus uses has a non-empty value;
   - the key set equals the bundle's moe.accounts.(signIn|usage|status|chip|vmTokenState).* keys (23 today);
   - each text's args count equals the number of distinct {n} placeholders in its value;
   - name missing or unknown keys and bad counts in the message.
Do not edit AccountPresentationTest.kt, AccountsPanel.kt or any other corpus.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff, the only review step.
- Would the test still pass if:
  - the weekly column took the first seven_day window instead of the busiest (C05);
  - percents were rounded instead of floored (C12's 89.6);
  - chips counted non-subscription accounts (C05, C12, C15);
  - +N more counted all accounts (C12);
  - spent did not win over active (C13);
  - times ignored the zone or the day (C12, C13);
  - check did not need the cli (C11);
  - the VM token actions treated an absent flag as false (C08)?
- Does the args type check really separate an Int from a String?
- Is every DoD case mapped to a named row (step 1's coverage list)?
- Is the corpus plain JSON with \u escapes, so VSC-13 replays it unchanged?
- Does the step 3 fix leave AccountPresentationTest green, and is it named in the summary?
- Run `git status --porcelain -- moe-jetbrains` and confirm the task touched only the two new files and AccountPresentation.kt.
- Peers own every other dirty path: never revert, stage or commit them.
- Report all three files in complete_step.modifiedFiles. Deleting /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc7-gate afterwards is fine; leave vsc7-architect for QA's audit.
